<title>UK: L-Bank plans 500 bln lire 2004 fungible bond.</title>
<headline>L-Bank plans 500 bln lire 2004 fungible bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Baden Wuerttemberg L-Finance NV, guaranteed by L-Bank, plans to launch a 500 billion lire bond, joint lead manager J.P. Morgan said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bond will be fungible with an existing parallel bond, maturing in March 2004. Other tranches are in marks and French francs with a 5.125 percent coupon.</p>
<p>The other joint lead manager is Caboto.</p>
<p>All tranches will be full fungible after being redenominated into euros when EMU is launched in 1999. --London newsroom,  +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
